<title>USA: Anheuser-Busch files $700 mln debt shelf.</title>
<headline>Anheuser-Busch files $700 mln debt shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anheuser-Busch Companies filed Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $700 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>Together with previously registered securities, the St. Louis-based beer company's shelf offering totals $750 million.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes. No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
